---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { longRuns } from "../data/long-run-tests";
---

<Page title="Long-run tests" description="How Ruvio behaves over hours of load and failures: what was tested, where, for how long, and the result.">
  <PageIntro title="Long-run tests">
    Short tests run in seconds on one machine. These runs keep a multi-node cluster under load for hours, break it on
    a schedule and then check every recorded operation against what the cluster holds at the end, or measure a whole
    machine as shards are added.
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="reading">
    <div class="wrap runs">
      {longRuns.map((run) => (
        <article class="panel run">
          <header class="run-head">
            <div>
              <p class="when">{run.date}</p>
              <h2>{run.title}</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="passed">Passed</span>
          </header>
          <dl class="facts">
            <div><dt>Where</dt><dd>{run.environment}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>How long</dt><dd>{run.duration}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="grid grid-2 lists">
            <div>
              <h3>Tested</h3>
              <ul>{run.tested.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Result</h3>
              <ul>{run.result.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}</ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}

      <div class="prose how">
        <h2>How a run works</h2>
        <p>
          Each run builds the server from source on fresh virtual machines, starts a coordinator and two replicated
          groups on three machines, and drives load from a fourth. Every operation is written to a history file with its
          outcome: acknowledged, refused, or unknown. Faults are injected and healed on a schedule, and after each one the
          cluster must agree on its primaries and take writes again. At the end every key is read back and the history
          is checked for lost, duplicated, invented and out-of-order writes and for stale reads.
        </p>
        <p>
          The tool, its plans and the machine templates are in{" "}
          <a href={`${site.github}/tree/dev/tests/soak`}>tests/soak</a>; anyone can run them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .runs { display: grid; gap: 22px; }
  .run { padding: 26px; display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .run-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; }
  .run-head h2 { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: 23px; }
  .when { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--faint); font-weight: 500; }
  .passed {
    flex: none; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 10px;
  }
  .passed::before { content: "✓ "; color: var(--accent); }
  .facts { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 32px; }
  .facts div { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .facts dt { color: var(--faint); font-size: 15px; }
  .facts dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-body); font-size: 15px; }
  .lists h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink); }
  .lists ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; color: var(--ink-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: var(--leading); }
  .lists li + li { margin-top: 6px; }
  .how { margin-top: 12px; }
  .how h2 { font-size: 21px; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .grid-2.lists { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .run { padding: 20px; }
  }
</style>
